msgid "Example that uses different output registers\n"
msgstr "Exemple qui utilise différents registres de sortie\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"v2-prim-options\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"v2-prim-options\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Options {#options}"
msgstr "Options {#options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Options are specified differently in the V2 primitives in these ways:\n"
msgstr ""
"Les options sont spécifiées différemment dans les primitives V2 de ces "
"manières :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`SamplerV2` and `EstimatorV2` now have separate options classes. You can see"
" the available options and update option values during or after primitive "
"initialization.\n"
msgstr ""
"`SamplerV2` et `EstimatorV2` ont maintenant des classes d'options "
"distinctes. Tu peux voir les options disponibles et mettre à jour les "
"valeurs des options pendant ou après l'initialisation de la primitive.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead of the `set_options()` method, V2 primitive options have the "
"`update()` method that applies changes to the `options` attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"Au lieu de la méthode `set_options()`, les options des primitives V2 ont la "
"méthode `update()` qui applique les changements à l'attribut `options`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you do not specify a value for an option, it is given a special value of "
"`Unset` and the server defaults are used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tu ne spécifies pas une valeur pour une option, elle reçoit une valeur "
"spéciale `Unset` et les valeurs par défaut du serveur sont utilisées.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For V2 primitives, the `options` attribute is the `dataclass` Python type.  "
"You can use the built-in `asdict` method to convert it to a dictionary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour les primitives V2, l'attribut `options` est du type Python `dataclass`."
" Tu peux utiliser la méthode intégrée `asdict` pour la convertir en "
"dictionnaire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options) for the list of available options.\n"
msgstr ""
"Consulte la [référence API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options) pour la liste des options disponibles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/*Verified EstimatorV2. 2/23 */}\n"
msgstr "{/*Verified EstimatorV2. 2/23 */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"from dataclasses import asdict\n"
"from qiskit_ibm_runtime import QiskitRuntimeService\n"
"from qiskit_ibm_runtime import EstimatorV2 as Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"from dataclasses import asdict\n"
"from qiskit_ibm_runtime import QiskitRuntimeService\n"
"from qiskit_ibm_runtime import EstimatorV2 as Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"service = QiskitRuntimeService()\n"
"backend = service.least_busy(operational=True, simulator=False)\n"
msgstr ""
"service = QiskitRuntimeService()\n"
"backend = service.least_busy(operational=True, simulator=False)\n"

